  "exact_fresh_AND_isometry": "The four-T relative-phase circuit followed by Sdag(t) sends |a,b,0> to |a,b,a*b> with phase1 for every a,b. Before Sdag the only nontrivial fresh-target phase is i on a=b=1. It is not a full Toffoli on dirty targets.",
  "exact_cleanup_Kraus_identity": "H then measurement outcome m on |a*b> gives (-1)^(m*a*b)/sqrt(2). CZ(a,b)^m cancels that sign, and X(t)^m resets the measured target. Every corrected branch is exactly I/sqrt(2) on inputs and any untouched entangled output/reference; the outcome is independent of quantum input.",
  "fulladder_boolean_identity": "a+b+c = (a XOR b XOR c) + 2*((a AND b) XOR ((a XOR b) AND c)). Compute both ANDs into fresh scratch, XOR them into dirty carry, XOR a XOR b XOR c into dirty sum. Erase second AND with current b'=a XOR b; restore b, then erase first AND with original a,b.",
  "fulladder_exact_channel_derivation": "Each cleanup contributes input-independent1/sqrt(2); four full branches have K_(m0,m1)=U/2 including scratch-zero output. Therefore their probabilities are exactly1/4 and sum K rho Kdag = U rho Udag, including arbitrary superposition or external-reference entanglement. Kraus verification checks input phases; basis permutations alone would be insufficient.",
